I don't have Microsoft's reported results for fiscal Q4 2026 (the quarter ended June 30, 2026), so this is an estimate rather than a reported figure.

My estimate starts from fiscal Q4 2025, when revenue was about $76.4 billion and gross profit about $52.0 billion, a gross margin of roughly 68%. I assumed about 15–17% revenue growth, which gives fiscal Q4 2026 revenue of roughly $88 billion. I also assumed the gross margin eases slightly to about 67–68%, because AI infrastructure costs are rising. That puts gross profit at roughly $59–60 billion, and I used about $59.5 billion.

